Jistan Idiot <jistanidiot@gmail.com> wrote:
> I think I finally figured this out.  It's not that my dungeon.def file
> was in the wrong format.  It's that dgn_comp requires the file to be
> named something.pdf.  I have no idea why this is true.  I just
> happened to noticed a file called dungeon.pdf.  When I renamed my
> modified dungeon.def to dungeon.pdf and ran dgn_comp on it everything
> worked.

Like Pat wrote in another post in the thread, you need to process the
.def file with "makedefs -e" to get the .pdf file. 

> So now my next question...
> Let's say I'd like Mine's End to have a downstairs which connects to a
